Third-party components distributed with or used by Echoback
==========================================================

Echoback itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). The components below are either
built into the container image or invoked by it. Nothing copyleft is linked into
Echoback's own code.

| Component                     | License                    | How it is used                          |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| whisper.cpp                   | MIT                        | Built from source; transcription engine |
| ggml                          | MIT                        | ML library inside whisper.cpp           |
| Whisper GGML model weights    | MIT                        | Downloaded at build time, baked in      |
| FastAPI                       | MIT                        | HTTP framework                          |
| Starlette                     | BSD-3-Clause               | ASGI toolkit under FastAPI              |
| uvicorn                       | BSD-3-Clause               | ASGI server                             |
| httpx                         | BSD-3-Clause               | Outbound webhook client                 |
| python-multipart              | Apache-2.0                 | Multipart form parsing                  |
| Python                        | PSF-2.0                    | Runtime                                 |
| ffmpeg                        | LGPL-2.1+ (GPL if so built)| CLI subprocess only, never linked       |

ffmpeg note
-----------
ffmpeg is installed from the Debian package repositories and invoked strictly as
an external command-line binary (`ffmpeg -i ... -ar 16000 -ac 1 -f wav ...`). It
is not linked as a library and no ffmpeg source or headers are compiled into
Echoback, so its LGPL/GPL terms do not extend to this project's MIT-licensed
code. The ffmpeg licence text ships with the ffmpeg package inside the image at
/usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/copyright.


